# Argocd apps

## Gate

Use when the user asks for Application status, sync health, resource tree,
events, managed resources, AppProject details, registered clusters, or
workload logs through Argo CD. Skip bare "GitOps" with no Argo CD /
Application ask. Load `argocd-sync` when the turn also mutates (sync,
resource action, create/update/delete).

Never invent an Application name, Application namespace, project name, or
cluster server. Resolve from MCP listing this turn or from an id the user
pasted.

## Prefer MCP

When an Argo CD MCP is ready, use these tools — do not invent a side CLI
or raw API client while MCP works:

| Need | Tool | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| List apps | `list_applications` | optional `search`, `limit`, `offset` |
| Get app | `get_application` | `applicationName`; optional `applicationNamespace` |
| Resource tree | `get_application_resource_tree` | health / sync children |
| App events | `get_application_events` | controller / sync events |
| Managed resources | `get_application_managed_resources` | filter with `kind` / `namespace` / `name` / `group` / `version` |
| Resource manifests | `get_resources` | `resourceRefs` (empty = all — prefer filters) |
| Resource events | `get_resource_events` | needs resource identity from tree |
| Workload logs | `get_application_workload_logs` | `resourceRef` + optional `container` |
| AppProject | `get_appproject` | `projectName` |
| Clusters | `list_clusters` | optional `server` / `name` filter |

Optional `argocdBaseUrl` on tools when the MCP is multi-instance — only when
the user named a base URL or the connection already implies it. Do not
guess private hostnames.

## Resolve the app

1. Prefer exact `applicationName` (+ namespace) the user named.
2. Else `list_applications` with a `search` substring when known.
3. Confirm with `get_application` before claiming Healthy / Synced /
   OutOfSync / Degraded.
4. If several apps match, list name + namespace + project + sync/health
   and ask once — do not pick prod by vibes.
5. Non-default Application namespaces: pass `applicationNamespace` on
   every follow-up call to avoid permission / not-found errors.

## Status and tree

1. Call `get_application` for sync status, health, source revision, and
   destination.
2. Use `get_application_resource_tree` when the ask is "what is broken"
   or which child is Degraded / Progressing / Missing.
3. Prefer filtered `get_application_managed_resources` over dumping every
   object when the app is large (token limits).
4. `get_application_events` / `get_resource_events` for recent sync or
   reconcile failures — summarize, do not paste secrets from event
   messages.
5. Workload logs via `get_application_workload_logs` only when the user
   asked for logs and you have a real `resourceRef` from the tree —
   never invent pod names. Keep excerpts short and redacted.

## Projects and clusters

- `get_appproject` when the ask is about allowed sources, destinations,
  or RBAC-shaped project limits — report the project name and constraints,
  not credentials.
- `list_clusters` to resolve destination cluster names/servers the user
  referred to vaguely. Never invent a cluster server URL.

## Honesty

- Do **not** claim Synced / Healthy without a fresh `get_application`
  (or tree) read this turn.
- Distinguish Desired vs Live when the payload exposes it; OutOfSync is
  not Healthy.
- Auto-sync enabled in the Application spec is not the same as "I just
  synced" — say which evidence you have.

## Report shape

1. Application name + namespace (+ project when known)
2. Sync status + health (+ revision / destination when cheap)
3. Failing child kind/name from the tree when degraded
4. Short event or log excerpt when it explains the failure (redacted)
5. Next action (wait, sync with explicit verb, fix source, or stop)

## Out of scope

- Raw cluster API triage without Argo CD Application context (pods,
  Deployments outside an Application) — stop or keep the answer at the
  Application boundary
- Site-specific app catalogs — resolve from MCP, never invent
- Mutating sync / create / delete / resource actions — see `argocd-sync`
